        "PMC6427779::chunk::002::material_and_methods::57f9c0f293"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Additive manufacturing or high-rate casting provides rapid solidification that promotes non-equilibrium structures in this alloy system.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6427779::chunk::002::material_and_methods::57f9c0f293"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding tungsten to NbMoTa increases the atomic-size mismatch.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding tungsten to NbMoTa increases the alloy's overall mixing entropy.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Atomic-size difference and mixing entropy are relevant criteria for phase formation in high-entropy alloys.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7513042::chunk::004::discussion::ef977a5008"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Increased atomic-size mismatch and mixing entropy slow crystallization kinetics during rapid solidification.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Tungsten has a high melting point.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6427779::chunk::002::material_and_methods::57f9c0f293"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Tungsten has a relatively larger atomic radius in the NbMoTa alloy context.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Tungsten-induced local strain raises the nucleation barrier for crystallization.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Tungsten addition reduces atomic diffusivity in NbMoTaW.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A higher crystallization barrier and lower diffusivity favor glass formation over crystalline ordering.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Rapidly cooled NbMoTaW should form more amorphous or glassy material than rapidly cooled NbMoTa.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Under slow cooling, tungsten addition may be insufficient to inhibit crystallization and produce a glassy structure.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Broader or absent crystalline XRD peaks and a discernible DSC glass transition can be used as evidence of increased amorphous-phase formation.",
